<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n56330" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">κεάζω</span></b> , 
			Ep.
		
		fut.
		<div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>A.</b>
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">κεάσσω</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Orph.
					<u>A.</u>
					849
				</span></i>
			: aor.
			
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">κέᾰσα, κέασσα, ἐκέασσα</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Hom.
				</span></i>
			 (v. infr.):—
				Pass.
			, aor.
			
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">κεάσθην</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Il.
					16.412
				</span></i>
			, but part.
			
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">κεᾰθείσης</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					<u>App.Anth.</u>
					3.167
				</span></i>
			: pf.
			part.
			<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">κεκεασμένος</span> (v.
				infr.):—<i>split, cleave</i> wood, 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">κέασε ξύλα νηλέϊ χαλκῷ</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Od.
					14.418
				</span></i>
			; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">κέασαν ξύλα</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					20.161
				</span></i>
			; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ξύλα . . νέον κεκεασμένα χαλκῷ</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					18.309
				</span></i>
			, cf. <i><span class="en">
				Hp.
				<u>Mul.</u>
				2.153
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				Call.
				<u>Fr.</u>
				289
			</span></i>, etc.; of lightning, <i>shiver</i>, 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">νῆα . . κεραυνῷ Ζεὺς ἔλσας ἐκέασσε</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Od.
					5.132
				</span></i>
			; of a spear, 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">κέασσε δ᾽ ἄρ᾽ ὀστέα λευκά</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Il.
					16.347
				</span></i>
			; [<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">κεφαλὴ] ἄνδιχα πᾶσα κεάσθη</span>
			<i>was cloven</i> in twain, ib.<i><span class="en">
				412
			</span></i>; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">κεκεασμένον εὐρέϊ κύκλῳ οὐρανόν</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Arat.
					474
				</span></i>
			. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense3"><b>2.</b>
			<i>pound, rub to pieces</i>, 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἢ σφέλᾳ ἢ ὅλμῳ κεάσας</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Nic.
					<u>Th.</u>
					644
				</span></i>
			. (<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">κεᾰ-ζω</span> fr. <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">κεᾰ</span>- in <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">κεᾰ-θείσης</span> (v. supr.), <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">εὐ-κέα-τος, κέαρνον</span>, and perh. <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">κείων</span>, 
				v.
				<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">κείω</span>
			 (B); perh. cf. Skt. <i>śásati</i>
			'cut', Lat. <i>castrare.</i>)</div>
